13. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] LaDou J. Current Occupational and Environmental Medicine . 4. McGraw-Hill Publishers, New York, NY; 2008. [ Google Scholar ] Health and Safety Executive (HSE) COSHH Essentials--easy steps to control chemicals (HSG 193) Sudbury: HSE Books; 1999. ISBN 0 7176 2421. [ Google Scholar ] Garrod ANI, Rajan Sithamparanadarajah R. Developing COSHH Essentials: Dermal Exposure, Personal Protective Equipment and First Aid. Ann Occup Hyg. 2003;47:577–588. doi: 10.1093/annhyg/meg089. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Mowe G, Gylseth B, Hartveit F, Skaug V. Occupational asbestos exposure, lung-fiber concentration and latency time in malignant mesothelioma. Scand J Work Environ Health. 1984;10:293–298. doi: 10.5271/sjweh.2326. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] CDC. Vynil Chloride (p. 18) http://www.atsdr.cdc.gov/toxprofiles/tp20-c2.pdf (accessed on 30 June 2010) Rosenstock L, Cullen MR. Clinical Occupational Medicine. WB Saunders Company, Philadelphia PA; 1986. [ Google Scholar ] Wexler P. The US National Library of Medicine Toxicology and Environmental Health Information Program. Toxicology. 2004;198:161–168. doi: 10.1016/j.tox.2004.01.037. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Fitzpatrick RB. Haz-Map: information on hazardous chemicals and occupational diseases. Medical Reference Services Quarterly. 2004;23(2):49–56. doi: 10.1300/J115v23n02_05. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] AJ, Anema JR, van der Wal G, van Mechelen W. Work-related disease in general practice: a systematic review. Family Practice. 2005;22:197–204. doi: 10.1093/fampra/cmh727. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Driscoll TR, Hendrie AL. Surveillance of work-related disorders in Australia using general practitioner data. Australian New Zeland Journal of Public Health. 2002;26:346–51. doi: 10.1111/j.1467-842X.2002.tb00183.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Won JU, Dembe AE. Services provided by family physicians for patients with occupational injuries an